{
  "title": "Ronda, Spain",
  "indexDescription": "A day in Ronda in the winter of 2009.",
  "description": "A day in Ronda in the winter of 2009.\n\nFrom Malaga on Dec 20th we stopped at Ronda on our way to Arcos.   Like Arcos, Ronda is an small old town on a hill with scenic white stucco houses and beautiful views of the countryside. \n\nAlex was telling us that Spain has BurgerKing fast food restaurants and they are fairly popular.  They pronounce it in a funny way and Alex as often heard saying it that way on the streets of Ronda.\n\nI was parallel parking on the left side on a small uphill street as we entered Ronda.  It took me several tries to get the van parked correctly in a tight spot.  This caused a big backup of cars behind us.  Alex was translating and I remember one comment from a passing car about \"you're a child\" referring to my slow parking job.",
